// A flag can display an image fetched from the internet. The server side of
// that is sound — the packet handler holds a hard allowlist
// (^https://i\.imgur\.com/…\.(png|jpeg|jpg|webp)$), checks that the player is
// the flag's owner, and refuses beyond 8 blocks. What it cannot check is what
// the picture shows, and every client in render range downloads it.
//
// Know what turning it off is worth: the gate that reads this key sits in
// FlagBlock inside an `if (level.isClientSide())` branch, which makes it a UI
// lock, not a server one. A modified client still gets through, and only
// CoreProtect will say who placed the flag.
//
// The six orbits are off because a space station is placed straight into the
// world by StructureTemplate — it fires no block-place event, and the only
// claim check Ad Astra makes is against Cadmus, which this pack does not run.
// Open Parties and Claims therefore has nowhere to hook in, and a station can
// be stamped over chunks somebody claimed and left empty. Ad Astra does stop a
// station being built within 2 chunks of an existing one, so the hole is
// narrow, but the fix is one key rather than a mixin.
//
// This key is a real server-side gate, whatever its own comment says:
// ModUtils.canTeleportToPlanet splits it and every one of the three packets —
// land, land on a station, construct a station — goes through that method.
// Staff still pass, via creative, spectator or permission level. Entries are
// compared with String.equals, so no spaces after the commas.
//
// Planets are untouched. Landing on one never involves a station: the rocket
// is swapped for a Lander that carries the player and the rocket's inventory
// down. Building and claiming happen on the surface, as everywhere else.
//
// Only the keys we change are listed. Resourceful Config fills the rest in
// from the mod's own defaults and rewrites the file with them.
{
  "rconfig:version": 0,
  "allowFlagImages": false,
  "disabledPlanets": "ad_astra:earth_orbit,ad_astra:moon_orbit,ad_astra:mars_orbit,ad_astra:venus_orbit,ad_astra:mercury_orbit,ad_astra:glacio_orbit"
}
